  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the latus rectum of the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> be the common chord to the circles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> each of them having radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>. Then, the distance between the centres of the circles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0089_844e8f48c68e.png\" style=\"width: 346px; height: 240px;\" /></p><p>Co-ordinates of focus of parabola will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Now, length of latus-rectum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;length of semi latus-rectum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Now, radius of circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now, applying pythagoras theorem in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>16</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
